NEARS-3539 AC2 (b) — live demonstration against the running admin panel
(LanguageController::update_default_status), NOT just the automated test.

Setup:
- Backend booted from THIS worktree (fix/NEARS-3539-backend-hygiene-cluster),
  `php artisan serve --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8010`, pointed at the shared
  multi_food_db (this call path makes ZERO writes on the negative branch —
  confirmed below — so it is safe on the shared dev DB without a private
  clone).
- Logged into the admin panel (admin@admin.com) via the Playwright-backed
  uinav_web driver (system python3 interpreter, package installed at
  /usr/bin/python3; the default python3 in this shell lacked the
  playwright package).
- No UI element exists to submit an arbitrary/unconfigured code (per the
  ticket note) — the "live" path taken instead builds and submits a REAL
  browser-native HTML form (method=POST, real _token from the page's
  <meta name="csrf-token">, browser-managed session cookies) against
  POST /admin/business-settings/language/update-default-status with
  code=zz-nonexistent-3539 (matches no configured system_language entry).
  This is a genuine authenticated browser request through the live running
  app, not a raw curl/API call bypassing the browser session.

Pre-state (read-only SELECT):
  mysql> SELECT value FROM business_settings WHERE key='system_language';
  [{"id":1,"direction":"ltr","code":"en","status":1,"default":true},
   {"id":"ar2","code":"ar","direction":"rtl","status":0,"default":false}]

Request: POST /admin/business-settings/language/update-default-status
  code=zz-nonexistent-3539 (no configured language has this code)

Result: 302 redirect back to /admin/business-settings/language (matches the
LanguageController's `return back();` on the !$matched branch).

Rendered flash toastr block on the redirected page (captured from raw page
HTML, the exact block injected by Toastr::message() in
resources/views/layouts/admin/app.blade.php):
  <script type="text/javascript">toastr.error('Something went wrong','');</script>

This is translate('messages.something_went_wrong') = "Something went wrong" —
the FAILURE toast added by the NEARS-3539 fix. Crucially, the SUCCESS toast
("Default Language Changed!") that the pre-fix code would have shown after
silently defaulting=false-ing every entry did NOT fire.

Post-state (read-only SELECT, unchanged):
  mysql> SELECT value FROM business_settings WHERE key='system_language';
  [{"id":1,"direction":"ltr","code":"en","status":1,"default":true},
   {"id":"ar2","code":"ar","direction":"rtl","status":0,"default":false}]

Confirms both halves of AC2(b): the existing default ("en") is preserved
byte-for-byte unchanged, AND the response reflects failure (error toast, not
the success toast).

Backend log (Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log): no new [FAIL]/[ERR] lines from
this request (checked immediately after, file mtime unchanged from the prior
phpunit run) — expected: this validation-style branch mirrors the existing
"already default" Toastr::warning branch a few lines up, neither of which is
backed by a Log:: call in this codebase's existing pattern; this is a
controlled business-validation response, not an unexpected system failure.

